	abstract = {{\textless}h3{\textgreater}Abstract{\textless}/h3{\textgreater} {\textless}p{\textgreater}We present \textit{KnockoffZoom}, a flexible method for the genetic mapping of complex traits at multiple resolutions. \textit{KnockoffZoom} localizes causal variants precisely and provably controls the false discovery rate using artificial genotypes as negative controls. Our method is equally valid for quantitative and binary phenotypes, making no assumptions about their genetic architectures. Instead, we rely on well-established genetic models of linkage disequilibrium. We demonstrate that our method can detect more associations than mixed effects models and achieve fine-mapping precision, at comparable computational cost. Lastly, we apply \textit{KnockoffZoom} to data from 350k subjects in the UK Biobank and report many new findings.{\textless}/p{\textgreater}},
